    "lawCode": "Amd §8, Chap 292 of 2007",
    "lawSection": "State Finance",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5659\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend chapter 292 of the laws of 2007 amending the state\nfinance law relating to state contracts with not-for-profit\norganizations, in relation to making permanent the effectiveness of\nsuch provisions\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThe purpose of this bill is to renew expiring provisions of the 2007\nlaw regarding non-for-profit contracts. The provisions of this bill\nallowing the comptroller to waive interest and penalties in unusual\ncircumstances are set to expire. This bill will make these provisions\npermanent.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 amends § 8 of chapter 292 of the laws of 2007 is amended to\nmake permanent changes allowing the comptroller to waive interest and\npenalties in unusual circumstances.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nNot-for-profit organizations have been finding themselves having to\nscramble to recover from late notification by agencies of intent not\nto renew contracts. When the notification does come, the NFP\nfrequently is in the position of having made expenditures in\nanticipation of contract renewal. Also, NFPs have been placed in\npositions of being required to waive their statutory right to interest\npayment from the agency in order to execute the contact. In 2007,\nchanges were made to make these procedures more effective. This bill\nmakes permanent the provisions allowing the comptroller oversight of\ndetermining when there are unusual circumstances allowing the state to\nwaive interest and penalties for having renewed the contract late\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nA.6018/S.2616 (2007). Signed into law.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nMinimal.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
